-- One statement per bug found while building P1-07. R1's mitigation: "Add every bug-producing
-- survey to fixtures/corpus/ permanently." Each of these round-trips today and each of them did
-- not at some point, so each is a guard against a specific regression rather than a general
-- smoke test.

-- Found by P5: both operands are literals, so neither can supply the other's domain. Printing bare
-- codes here re-parsed as `num` and silently changed the comparison's type.
IF [Q5.Apple] CONTAINS 1 THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P6: a COALESCE takes its type from the same expectation its arms do, so the resolver has
-- to look through it when deciding which side of a comparison to resolve first.
IF COALESCE(AGE_BAND.1, AGE_BAND.2) = 1 THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P1: `and`/`or` are n-ary (D §2.3) and nested same-operator nodes are flattened by the
-- compiler's optimizer (D §10.1), not by the parser. Without the parentheses the reparse flattens
-- three operands into one node and T1 fails.
IF S1 = 1 OR (Q6 > 1 OR AGE > 2) THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P1: `--` is a comment marker, so an unparenthesized double negation turned the rest of
-- the line into a comment and the statement lost its condition.
IF -(-Q6) > 0 THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P1: a bare action's trailing IF has to be on the same line, or the action swallows the
-- IF of the rule below it. Both statements here are separate.
HIDE Q12 IF S1 = 1
IF S1 = 2 THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P1: a scalar question emits a variable with its own name (schema §1), so `ANSWERED(Q12)`
-- is ambiguous between the variable and the question. The bare form is the variable.
IF ANSWERED(QUESTION Q12) AND ANSWERED(Q12) THEN SHOW Q12

-- Found by P3: `==` is accepted as an assignment operator, because a programmer arriving from
-- JavaScript types it and the printer normalizes it to `=` anyway.
SET HEAVY_BUYER = TRUE

-- Found by P1: a derived enum variable has a domain and no question, so there is no `Q5.Apple`
-- spelling for its codes. `AGE_BAND.2` is how a code in that domain is written.
SET AGE_BAND = AGE_BAND.2

-- Found by P6: `MIN_OF` over a matrix's rows is `enum<scale>`, not `num` (D §3.3: `agg(min|max) : τ`
-- where τ is the element type). The projection is what makes it numeric.
IF MIN_OF(ROWS OF Q7 SELECT item.code) >= 3 THEN SHOW Q12

-- An unresolvable reference prints back as itself rather than as NULL: a formatter that rewrote a
-- typo would be deleting the author's work. This statement therefore carries an LGC-T001, on
-- purpose, and is excluded from the corpus test's "no errors" assertion.
IF NOT_A_VARIABLE = 1 THEN SHOW Q12
